From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:47:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] OS-0: futex, TLS, clocks, stat/rename/chdir, spawn/wait,
 environment

syscall.h gains the kernel's new calls (SYS_FUTEX, SYS_CLOCK, SYS_STAT,
SYS_RENAME, SYS_CHDIR, SYS_SPAWN, SYS_WAIT, the SYS_THREAD FS-base and
CREATE_EX operations, SYS_ERR_TIMEDOUT). thread.h adds futex wait/wake,
the FS base and mos_thread_create_ex with a futex join. process.h is new:
spawn, wait, getenv and small file/time helpers. crt0 keeps the
environment in environ and passes it to main as a third argument.

programs/os0test is the self-test the kernel's make ci-os0 runs in QEMU;
it passes there (252 checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
